                "reviews": [
                    {
                        "recommendationid": "235956248",
                        "author": {
                            "steamid": "76561199330750233",
                            "num_reviews": 3,
                            "playtime_forever": 432,
                            "playtime_last_two_weeks": 0,
                            "playtime_at_review": 432,
                            "last_played": 1785789859
                        },
                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "I have played through this game only once playing each level only once, which I'm sure is rather shocking looking at the amount of hours I've put into this game, but what can I say? I'm a video game enjoyer, not a gamer. Games like this one, which require conventional skill in playing video games, are games that I don't tend to be very good at. When it comes to platformer games, modern Mario and Sonic are more paygrade. However, despite having hundreds of deaths on levels that others can not only beat in one try, but speedrun repeatedly getting increasingly better times, I very much enjoyed this game. The game requires quick thinking and precision for sure, so if you like that sort of thing, you should definitely give the game a try. There is no controller support as far as other reviews are saying, which may be a turnoff for some, but I didn't notice that there was no controller support because the mouse and keyboard just worked so well for this game that I never even thought to try controller, and this is coming from a person who has played VERY FEW platformers on mouse and keyboard.",
